From: clawd20130 <clawd20130@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 03:11:02 +0900
Subject: freedreno: dma-buf sharing on KGSL (LINEAR), gralloc UBWC
 import on request

With FD_KGSL_ENABLE_DMABUF=1 the KGSL backend shares buffers with other processes (clients and the
compositor) as dma-bufs from /dev/dma_heap/system:
- the screen reports dma-buf import and export (KGSL is not DRM: no DRM_CAP_PRIME);
- shared and scanout resources are LINEAR, the only layout exported or queried as a modifier;
- exporting a native KGSL resource that was not allocated shared reallocates it shared (shadow)
  first, since only dma-heap memory can be exported;
- an imported dma-buf is shared already, so exporting it again hands out the same buffer.
  Without this, GBM's import then get_fd (Xwayland on a DRI3 client's buffer) gave a new, empty
  buffer and X11 GL windows stayed black;
- FD_KGSL_DMABUF_UBWC=1 also accepts importing DRM_FORMAT_MOD_QCOM_COMPRESSED buffers allocated by
  the platform gralloc. fdl6's UBWC layout matches gralloc's RGBA8888_UBWC, and the kernel programs
  the UBWC mode for the whole GPU (docs/57). Exports and modifier queries stay LINEAR;
- timestamp queries on KGSL, which reports no max_freq (the tick rate is fixed).

This is the lfdevs/mesa-for-android-container branch's KGSL dma-buf contract (its PR #85) with
this project's UBWC import (docs/57) and import-is-shared fix (docs/research/93) folded in, and
without its XWAYLAND_FORCE_KGSL_SURFACELESS alias for PRoot.

Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-09-30
X-Rungic-Status: Pending [KGSL only; carried]
X-Rungic-Tests: L3:perf.compositor (KWin UBWC outputs), L3:xwayland.kgsl-glamor (import then export keeps the inode)
X-Rungic-Docs: docs/57, docs/research/93, docs/research/94
